{{also|Jerk}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdʒɜːk/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdʒɜɹk/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-jerk.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)k|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{inh|en|enm|yerk||sudden motion}} and {{der|en|enm|yerkid|t=tightly pulled}}, from {{der|en|ang|ġearc||ready, active, quick}} and {{inh|en|ang|ġearcian|t=to prepare, make ready, procure, furnish, supply}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|yerk|t=to jerk}}. Related also to {{m+|en|yare|t=ready}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|en|yark}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sudden]], often uncontrolled [[movement]], especially of the body.
#* '''1856''', {{w|Gustave Flaubert}}, {{w|Madame Bovary}}, Part III Chapter X, translated by Eleanor Marx-Aveling
#*: The black cloth bestrewn with white beads blew up from time to time, laying bare the coffin. The tired bearers walked more slowly, and it advanced with constant '''jerks''', like a boat that pitches with every wave.
#* {{RQ:Chesterton Thursday|page=114|passage=A barrel-organ in the street suddenly sprang with a '''jerk''' into a jovial tune.}}
# A quick [[tug]] or shake.
#: {{ux|en|When I yell "OK," give the mooring line a good '''jerk'''!}}
# {{lb|en|originally|North America|slang|pejorative}} A person with [[unlikable]] or [[obnoxious]] qualities and behavior, typically [[mean]], [[self-centered]]{{,}} or [[disagreeable]]; an [[asshole]].
#* {{quote-av|en|actor=w:Angela Lansbury|role=Eleanor Iselin|writer=w:George Axelrod|title={{w|The Manchurian Candidate (1962 film)|The Manchurian Candidate}}|year=1962|time=1:23:39|passage=Oh, Raymond―don't be such a '''jerk'''. Go and get yourself a drink or a tranquilizer or something.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|speaker={{w|Norm Macdonald}}|title={{w|Norm Macdonald Live}}|year=2013|season=1|number=3|passage=And [Albert Fish] was dizzyingly happy about it, smiled as described the grizzly details of the tortures and the murders, appearing to the detectives and  one of the detectives said "he appeared as the Devil himself." I mean this Albert F-, I mean this guy was a real '''jerk'''!}}
#: {{ux|en|I finally fired him, because he was being a real '''jerk''' to his customers, even to some of the staff.}}
#: {{ux|en|You really are a '''jerk''' sometimes.}}
# {{lb|en|US|slang|pejorative}} A [[stupid]] person; an [[idiot]] or [[fool]].<!-- (This meaning is given in the American Heritage Dictionary of 1969 whereas the previous meaning is not.)-->
# {{lb|en|weightlifting}} A [[lift]] in which the weight is taken with a quick motion from shoulder height to a position above the head with arms fully extended and held there for a brief time.
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[masturbation|Masturbation]].
## {{lb|en|internet slang}} An act of [[satirize|satirizing]] behavior that is, to an extent, [[common]] in a community, especially in [[circlejerk]] [[subreddit|subreddits]].
##: {{ux|en|'''Jerk''' of the Year contender}}
# {{lb|en|preceded by definite article}} A [[dance]], popular in Western culture in the 1960s, in which the head and upper body is thrown forwards regularly to the beat of the music.
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist={{w|Don Julian}}|title=The Jerk|artist={{w|The Larks}}|year=1964|text=Girls, hey, what's that you're doing<br>Girl, girl, what's that you're doing<br>You got to show me the steps to it<br>Somehow, gonna learn how to do it<br>Doing the '''jerk'''<br>Hey, do the '''jerk'''<br>Girl, come on and work<br>Hey, do the '''jerk'''.}}
# {{lb|en|physics|engineering}} The rate of [[change]] in [[acceleration]] with respect to [[time]].
# {{lb|en|US|obsolete}} A [[soda jerk]].

=====Usage notes=====
{{wikipedia|Jerk (physics)}}
* Jerk is measured in [[metre]]s per [[second]] [[cube]]d (m/s<sup>3</sup>) in [[SI]] units, or in [[feet]] per second cubed (ft/s<sup>3</sup>) in [[imperial]] units.

